      "pins": ["U1.10 (BS0)"],
      "nets": ["VCC"],
      "observed": "On the display sheet, SSD1306 pin 10 (BS0) is wired to VCC.",
      "expected": "The specification says BS0 is tied to GND, BS1 to VCC, and BS2 to GND for I2C mode.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "\"BS0 10\" and \"VCC\"; the pin-10 wire joins the VCC rail (display sheet, page 3)."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "\"BS0 (pin 10) → GND; BS1 (pin 11) → VCC; BS2 (pin 12) → GND\" (§3, Display)."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The interface-selection straps do not match the specified I2C configuration, so the OLED may select a different interface mode and fail to communicate with the MCU.",
      "confidence": 0.78
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The display sheet appears to strap SSD1306 BS0 (pin 10) to VCC, contrary to the specified GND connection for I2C mode. This can select the wrong interface mode and prevent normal display communication."
}

